 "spec": "Vocabulary ids: 0 <pad>, 1 <bos>, 2 <eos>, 3 ' ', 4 ',', 5 '.', 6 '!', 7 '?', 8 \"'\", 9 '\"', 10..35 = a..z (a=10, e=14, i=18, o=24, u=30, y=34). Input ctx [8,36]: one-hot rows, oldest first, row 7 = most recent token; an all-zero row means 'before document start'. LETTER row = token in 10..35. BOUNDARY row = an all-zero row, or a row whose token is not a letter and is not the apostrophe (id 8) [so bos, space, , . ! ? and the double quote are boundaries; the apostrophe is NOT]. 'word so far' = the maximal run of LETTER rows ending at row 7 (or at the row named in the rule); it is 'anchored' when the row just before the run exists and is a BOUNDARY row. Evidence output y [36] is added to next-token logits by the parent, in nats; 0 means 'no opinion'. Entries for ids 0,1 must be exactly 0 unless a rule says otherwise; id 2 (<eos>) is 0 unless a rule says otherwise. Case 'note' fields explain the case; 'expect' vectors are index 0..35 in vocabulary order and must be matched within tol. Inputs are exact one-hot / 0-1 values. Tables in 'data' are authoritative and must not be changed. You may write a helper script that expands 'data' into proposal JSON. Each cell/param holds at most 40 numbers (spread lookups over many cells and combine with ops; ops on ctx rows such as slice/mul/sum are exact and free of parameters).\n\nQuotation dynamics. Inputs ctx and q (q = 1 iff currently inside a quotation, ALREADY updated for row 7: right after an opening quote token q=1). Let p = the token in row 7. y is the SUM of:\n E:  if q >= 0.5: y[<eos>] += -6.\n R1: q>=0.5 and p is the double quote (just opened): add data.qopen letters; y['\"'] += -3; y[' '] += -3; y[','] += -2; y['.'] += -2.\n R2: q<0.5 and p is the double quote (just closed): y[' '] += 0.8, y[','] += 0.3, y['.'] += 0.4, y['\"'] += -3, and -1.5 to all 26 letters.\n R3: q>=0.5 and p in , . ! ?: y['\"'] += 1.0 / 0.6 / 1.6 / 1.6 respectively (closing quote likely).\n R4: q<0.5 and p is space and row 6 is ',': y['\"'] += 0.4; plus 2.1 more if row 5 is the letter 'd' (said, asked, ...); plus 0.6 more if row 5 is the letter 'm' (mom, ...).\n R5: q<0.5 and p is space and row 6 is one of . ! ?: y['\"'] += 0.8.\n R6: q>=0.5 and p is space: y['\"'] += -2.5.\nEverything else 0 (E and R1 both apply just after an opening quote). Ids 0,1 are 0. It is a small case analysis on rows 5-7 and q.",
